From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Garcia-Madico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:39:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcn-bt-slim: keep the stream startup look for
 the chip short

With the offloaded SCO up the WCN6750 answers the first query ("enumerated
at stream startup after 0 ms"), so waiting in startup only matters when the
SCO is not there yet, and then it does not help. It happens at the start of
a call: the session manager puts the card on the Bluetooth ports before the
call supervisor has brought the SCO up. Waiting 5 s there, once for each
direction, held the card long enough for every pactl the supervisor ran to
time out, and it gave up on its first attempt (measured on the Nothing Phone
(1) with kernel r123).

Look for 500 ms and fail fast. The supervisor then brings the SCO up and
moves the card to the headset again, and that start finds the chip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c
index 494e975b8..1fab6109d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c
@@ -119,14 +119,21 @@
  * later suspends.
  *
  * So at boot only a short quiet poll, as before, in case the chip is already
- * there. The real look happens when a stream starts - the SCO is up by then -
- * with the controller held, for up to WCN_STARTUP_LADDR_TRIES *
- * WCN_STARTUP_LADDR_POLL_MS, which is also where the vendor driver looks for
- * the chip.
+ * there. The real look happens when a stream starts, with the controller held,
+ * which is also where the vendor driver looks for the chip.
+ *
+ * Kept short, and failing fast. With the offloaded SCO up the chip answers at
+ * once ("enumerated at stream startup after 0 ms"). Without it, waiting does
+ * not help, and it hurts: at the start of a call the session manager can put
+ * the card on the Bluetooth ports before the SCO exists, and a 5 s wait here,
+ * once per direction, held the card long enough for every pactl in the call
+ * supervisor to time out (measured 2026-09-13, kernel r123). Failing fast
+ * lets the supervisor bring the SCO up and put the card on the headset again,
+ * and that second start finds the chip.
  */
 #define WCN_LADDR_TRIES			20
 #define WCN_LADDR_POLL_MS		250
-#define WCN_STARTUP_LADDR_TRIES		250
+#define WCN_STARTUP_LADDR_TRIES		25
 #define WCN_STARTUP_LADDR_POLL_MS	20
 
 struct wcn_bt_slim {
-- 
2.47.3

